Now combat.js. Need `pointSegDist`? not needed. Imports: clamp, dist, TAU, angleLerp, Rng? use game.rng. TOOLS from config; resolveCollisions.

Let me carefully implement.

Helper angleDiff:
```
const angleDelta = (a,b) => Math.atan2(Math.sin(b-a), Math.cos(b-a));
```

Player attack:
```
export function attack(game) {
 const p=game.player, tool=TOOLS[p.tool];
 if (game.mode!=='play'||p.dead||p.atkCd>0) return;
 if (p.stamina < tool.stamina) { game.ui.toast('You are too winded.', 'danger', 1600); return; }
 if (!tool.melee) {
   if (p.arrows <= 0) { game.ui.toast('Your quiver is empty. Whittle more arrows in the craft panel.', 'danger', 2600); return; }
 }
 p.atkCd = tool.cd; p.stamina -= tool.stamina; p.atkAnim = 0.22; p.swingAngle = p.angle;
 game.audio.sfx(tool.melee?'swing':'bow');
 if (!tool.melee) {
   p.arrows--; game.projectiles.push({...});
   game.addParticles('spark', ...)? 
   if (game.ui) game.ui.updateResources(game);
   return;
 }
 // melee
 const reach = tool.range;
 const arc = tool.arc;
 let hitCount=0;
 for enemies alive...:
   d = dist; if (d <= reach + e.r) and angle abs < arc/2:
     crit = p.sneak && !e.aggro && tool.id !== 'axe'? Use all.
     dmg = tool.dmg * (crit?2.2:1) * (1 + random*0.1);
     damageEnemy(game, e, dmg, 'melee', crit);
     hitCount++;
 for animals...
   if dist < reach+14 && angle → a.hp -= tool.dmg; a.hit=.2; blood; if hp<=0 killAnimal;
 for props...
   nearest within reach+ maybe; angle diff < 1.2
 // swing particles
 const tipx = p.x + cos(p.angle)*reach*0.7...
 game.addParticles('dust', tipx,tipy, 2,{...});
 if (hitCount===0) maybe nothing
}
```
For animals bow arrows need handling in projectile.

Props: choose closest tree/rock and hit. Use filtering per swing:
```
let best=null,bd=1e9;
for prop of world.props if (!done && kind in ['pine','oak','dead','rock','stump'?]) {d... if d<reach+prop.r+18 && abs(angle)<1.25 && d<bd) best}
if best hitProp
```
`hitProp`:
- tree: dmg = tool axe?1:0.75; hp-=; leaves. if done: wood gain 3 or 4; record; float; sound.
- dead: hp2; wood 2.
- rock: hp 3; stone gain 2 per hit? Currently E mining gives 2/hit. For axe hit, give 1 stone per hit; if done +2. Keep: stone +=1 each hit; on complete +2 extra. Fine.
- stump gives wood? no.
Record text only when felled (not each hit), to avoid spam.
- add float "+N wood".

Projectiles:
```
function solidHit(game,x,y) {
 const grid=game.world.colGrid, cell=game.world.colCell;
 ...
 for c of list: if c.prop && (c.prop.done || c.prop.kind==='garden'||c.prop.kind==='lantern') continue; if dist< c.r*0.9+2 return true;
}
```
Arrows hit village crates/huts (colliders). Fine.

`updateProjectiles`:
```
for i projectile:
 life-=dt; if <=0 remove;
 steps? Speed 700 * dt 0.016 = 11px per frame; fine no tunneling with r~18.
 x+=vx*dt...
 if out → remove
 if solidHit → remove + particles
 if from player:
   for enemies: dist < e.r+6 → damageEnemy source arrow; remove; break
   for animals: ... kill
 else:
   if dist to player < p.r+5 → hurtPlayer(game,dmg); remove
```
Arrow hit enemy: damageEnemy must record bow traits; pass source 'arrow'.
- damageEnemy uses `byPlayer=true` assumption; enemy arrows don't call.

Enemy update:
- spawnT.
- `e.walk += dt`.
- state variables.
- Use `hasLineOfSight`? import from world. Check aggro LOS every 0.4s; but line of sight function uses grid lists and can be expensive. With 5 enemies * every 0.4s, fine.
- Since enemies spawn outside village and player in open, LOS rarely blocks.

